{
  "$comment": [
    "Conformance vectors for claude-remember's session-directory slug.",
    "",
    "THIS FILE IS GENERATED. Do not hand-edit it: run `python3 -m tests.slug_vectors`.",
    "Every expected value here was produced by running scripts/lib-slug.sh, and",
    "tests/test_slug_vectors_294.py regenerates the whole file on every CI run and",
    "fails if the checked-in bytes differ. It therefore cannot drift from the",
    "implementation without our own suite going red — which is the point: an",
    "external port that diffs against this file is diffing against something we",
    "are already holding still.",
    "",
    "Each vector:",
    "  id        - stable name. Suffixed .cygpath / .no-cygpath where the two differ.",
    "  path      - the input, when it is valid UTF-8. null when it is not.",
    "  path_b64  - the input as raw bytes, base64. ALWAYS present, and authoritative.",
    "  slug      - the expected result. Always ASCII [A-Za-z0-9-].",
    "  cygpath   - agnostic: same answer whether or not cygpath is on PATH.",
    "              present:  only holds with cygpath (an MSYS path being converted).",
    "              absent:   only holds without it.",
    "  truncated - true when the slug passed 200 characters and carries a hash.",
    "  requires  - what must be available to reproduce this with the shell version.",
    "  note      - why the case is here.",
    "",
    "If you are porting: the vectors you want are cygpath=agnostic and",
    "cygpath=absent. Those describe the pure function - fold a leading upper-case",
    "ASCII drive letter, replace every non-[A-Za-z0-9] UTF-16 CODE UNIT with a",
    "dash (so an astral character costs two), and past 200 characters keep the",
    "first 200 and append base36(abs(int32(hash))) of the ORIGINAL path.",
    "The cygpath=present vectors describe what the shell does to an MSYS-shaped",
    "path on its way in, and they are generated against a MODEL of cygpath",
    "(tests/cygpath_stub.py), not a real one.",
    "",
    "Vectors requiring 'utf8-decoder' are ill-formed UTF-8. The shell only",
    "consults the decoder where such a path can exist - on Linux always,",
    "elsewhere only under REMEMBER_UTF8_STRICT=1, which is how these were",
    "generated. A Windows port can ignore them: Windows paths come from UTF-16."
  ],
